.TH pepe-export 1  pepe "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pepe\-export \- Turn a JSON report into a page, a Markdown summary, text or CSV
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpepe export\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR] [\fB\-\-open\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIREPORT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turn a JSON report into a page, a Markdown summary, text or CSV
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Where it goes, its format from its extension; beside the report by default
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
The format when \-o doesn\*(Aqt say: html (the default), json, md, txt, csv, or all
.TP
\fB\-\-open\fR
Open it once written
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREPORT\fR>
The JSON report: a run\*(Aqs (\-\-json, \-\-snapshot, a recorded run), a ramp\*(Aqs or a ping\*(Aqs
